  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe wire cover check restores the upstream strict 0.002 mm tolerance for all current polygon inputs.\nThe repair removes the allowance that inferred meshed rounds from vertex coordinates.\n\nThe review found a sharp 16-sided R0.5 polygon that passed every classifier guard.\nIts path leaves about 0.0032 mm at each corner, above the cover tolerance.\nThe generator receives points without reliable arc or mesh provenance.\nIt cannot safely distinguish that polygon from a tessellated arc.\n\nThe original coarse-fillet acceptance remains deferred until reliable provenance reaches the cover check.\nFine facets that meet the strict tolerance can still pass.\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/3208-wire-facet-rounds.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe eight tests in `crates/motion/src/wire_edm/facet_tests.rs` include:\n\n- `a_small_drawn_polygon_with_facet_sized_turns_stays_refused`: the new R0.5 regression checks the inside-corner diagnostic and 0.0032 mm remainder.\n- `a_drawn_polygon_with_facet_sized_turns_stays_refused`: the existing R5 polygon remains refused.\n- `coarse_fillets_without_arc_provenance_stay_refused`: coarse r0.25, r0.5, and r0.165 fillets remain refused without provenance.\n- `a_fine_fillet_within_the_cover_tolerance_is_cut`: the r0.25 fillet with 30 facets remains accepted.\n\nMutation check: restore the reviewed cover allowance and classifier; the new R0.5 regression fails because the generator returns a toolpath.\nRestore the fix; the regression passes. All eight facet tests pass.\n\nFinal head: `11c8ed2625e8abc667222f1cdb5eba2fd0295d22`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, all 12 steps pass on the final head.\nMotion lib: 498 pass, 10 ignored. Motion `wire_fans`: 7 pass.\nApp: `golden_cl` 33, `wire_4axis` 8, `wire_burnout` 3, `wire_contour` 8, `wire_post` 12, `wire_tabs` 4, `wire_taper` 10, `wire_taper_angle` 5 pass.\nInitial attempts had missing-crate errors in cached artifacts. A clean worktree rebuild with the compiler cache disabled passed.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN on the final head.\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN on the final head. All 236 steps pass in 31.0 minutes.\nThe run reaches every motion and app heavy target:\n\n| Lane | Steps | Ignored tests passed |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Shared release build | 1 | — |\n| Motion heavy: lib, bins, integrations, doc, and known-failure checks | 37 | 59 |\n| App heavy: lib, bins, integrations, doc, and known-failure checks | 198 | 43 |\n\nThere are no unexpected failures.\nThe six declared known-failure checks validate their expected assertions: three for #1950 and three for #2849.\nThe compiler cache is disabled for this run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe issue's real STEP parts (EDM-T1..T3) did not run through MCP.\nThe synthetic profiles exercise the cover check directly.\n\nChangelog: The wire cover check refuses small drawn polygons that the inferred-round allowance previously accepted.\n\nRefs #3208\n",
